PROBE 1, NEGATIVE (real 62 -> 70; multiset 4t -> 2t; fresh fuzzy 90.1959 -> 82.2165 = -7.98; CONFLICT arbitrated on fuzzy, reverted) -- the argument-evaluation-order axis v1 named as untried. Target computes the second argument EARLY (`subf r4,r7,r4` at +0x134, before the crclr and before the rgb finalization) while we defer it past the whole argument set-up to +0x14c, so the second argument was hoisted to its own statement ahead of the rgb expression:
            y = L[2] - h / 2;
            rgb = (*(s32*)(base + 236) & 0xFF) |
                  ((*(s32*)(base + 228) & 0xFF) << 16) |
                  ((*(s32*)(base + 232) & 0xFF) << 8);
            DrawStringText(x, y, OPTCTL_FONT, rgb, msg, i);
  (plus `s32 y;` added to the declaration block)
  WHAT IT ACTUALLY DID: it closed the residual it aimed at -- the target-only `mr` and one of the two `addi` disappeared, taking the multiset from 4t to 2t -- but it displaced the rgb web hard enough to cost 8 points of fuzzy. The named cluster is reachable; the cost of reaching it this way is not payable.

PROBE 2, NEGATIVE (real 62 -> 64, multiset unchanged at 4t, +0x78 row UNCHANGED, reverted) -- the +0x78 axis v1 named as untried. Target emits `li r27,0` where we emit `addi r29,r30,0`, i.e. MWCC copies i's zero into off instead of materializing a fresh zero; split the comma initializer so off's zero cannot be CSE'd from i:
        off = 0;
        for (i = 0; i < 16; i++, off += 12) {
  (was: `for (i = 0, off = 0; i < 16; i++, off += 12) {`)
  WHY IT LOST: the +0x78 row did not move at all -- the copy is a register-allocator coalescing decision taken after both values are known to be zero, not a source-order effect -- and the split cost 2 real elsewhere.
